  "cards": [
    {
      "dot": "cyan",
      "title": "One process, two content paths",
      "items": [
        "Everything runs in one Express process (server/index.ts) over one Postgres.",
        "The canonical chain is ResearchJob → Story → Opportunity → Artifact → Publication → Result.",
        "A second older path (routes.ts + autopilot + discover) owns most live decisions and publishes through its own cron."
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "amber",
      "title": "Where decisions really live",
      "items": [
        "The Decision OS now has ten types; seven decide live and three legacy scores run in shadow mode.",
        "All of it is still gated by JEV_DECISION_ENGINE_ENABLED, default off.",
        "Shadow mode records JC-01 viral, JC-02 discover and JC-03 agent routing without acting on them."
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "emerald",
      "title": "Hard gates the code owns",
      "items": [
        "Only approved artifacts are schedulable or publishable; content is immutable at insert.",
        "providerCalled means no blind retry; ambiguous outcomes become outcome:\"unknown\".",
        "Auto-publish needs an explicit trusted + on_approval policy pair."
      ]
    }
  ]
